g 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.framework.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   41895 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.lsp.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   77739 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.target.blockdoc.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   46980 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.target.fatblock.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   40548 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.target.xsd.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   15146 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.workspace.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff  143886 Sep  3 00:13 package-lock.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff    3003 Sep  3 00:10 package.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@  18 pksoftware  staff     576 Sep  3 00:06 packages\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 pksoftware  staff     160 Aug 20 04:36 schemas\ndrwxr-xr-x@   9 pksoftware  staff     288 Aug 22 22:36 scripts\ndrwxr-xr-x@   7 pksoftware  staff     224 Aug 20 04:58 tests\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff     432 Aug 19 21:29 tsconfig.base.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff     637 Sep  3 00:10 tsconfig.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff     223 Aug 19 23:43 vitest.config.ts\nUsage: blockml &lt;command> [options]\n       blockml --help\n\nblockml is the BlockML toolchain CLI.\n\nBML is the editable source of truth. Companions (TypeScript, HTML, XSD, …) are derived.\nChange BML first, then compile or edit companions to match. Do not invent model semantics.\n\nInvocation: npx blockml &lt;command>\nDo not install or upgrade @blockml/cli unless asked. If the CLI is missing, run npm ci.\nIf @blockml/cli is not a project dependency, report that and stop.\n\nDiscover the model with the CLI, not grep:\n  search    where something is (find FQNs)\n  inspect   give me this Block already resolved (effective members)\n  graph     how it connects (inheritance, uses, used-by)\nGeneric grep, find, and file reads remain allowed. They are not the first way into the model.\n\nWorkflow:\n  task → search → FQNs → inspect (graph if structure) → targeted BML read → smallest BML edit → validate\n       → update companions to match (compile and/or edit)\n\nCommands:\n  search      Find FQNs. Corpus is validate --all.\n              blockml search &lt;query> [--json] [--limit n]\n              blockml search index [--force]\n  inspect     Resolved Block JSON (effective members).\n              blockml inspect &lt;fqn> [--depth n]\n  graph       Inheritance, uses / used-by, members, paths.\n              blockml graph uses|used-by|neighbors|ancestors|descendants|members &lt;fqn>\n              blockml graph path &lt;from> &lt;to>\n              blockml graph query &lt;cypher> | schema | index\n  new         Create a Block .bml and export it from the owning Library.\n              blockml new &lt;fqn> [--baseType FQN] [--is text]\n  validate    Parser + semantic check. Default: project sources, not npm.\n              blockml validate [--all] [&lt;file>]\n  compile     Render derived output for a registered target.\n              blockml compile blockdoc|xsd|fatblock\n  transform   Run a pending ModelTransformation.\n              blockml transform apply &lt;execution-fqn>\n\nShared flags: --src dir, --libraries a,b, --json, --help / -h\nCorpus for search, inspect, and graph is the same as validate --all.\nExit codes: 0 success, 1 diagnostic errors, 2 usage or configuration error.\n\nRun `blockml &lt;command> --help` for flags, defaults, output, and constraints.&quot;,&quot;is_error&quot;:false}]},&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;5d8689b9-d089-4adb-9dfa-a82710b1ec49&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;583ab723-59e1-42d4-a795-be73aaeebd8a&quot;,&quot;timestamp&quot;:&quot;2026-09-04T00:15:30.341Z&quot;,&quot;tool_use_result&quot;:{&quot;stdout&quot;:&quot;total 1928\ndrwxr-xr-x   38 pksoftware  staff    1216 Aug 30 00:00 .\ndrwxr-xr-x   23 pksoftware  staff     736 Aug 23 00:38 ..\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff    8196 Jul  6 20:12 .DS_Store\ndrwxr-xr-x    6 pksoftware  staff     192 Sep  4 02:15 .blockml\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 pksoftware  staff      96 Jul 10 01:37 .cursor\ndrwxr-xr-x   17 pksoftware  staff     544 Sep  4 02:15 .git\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 pksoftware  staff      96 Aug 22 22:36 .github\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff      68 Aug 28 00:26 .gitignore\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 pksoftware  staff      96 Aug 20 03:49 .vscode\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff    2720 Sep  3 02:47 AGENTS.md\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff   11350 Aug 22 22:35 LICENSE\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff    3060 Aug 26 21:05 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x    7 pksoftware  staff     224 Aug 26 23:27 blockdoc\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 pksoftware  staff      96 Sep  3 00:00 blocks\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff     351 Aug 20 04:36 catalog.xml\ndrwxr-xr-x   29 pksoftware  staff     928 Aug  2 00:23 docs\ndrwxr-xr-x  199 pksoftware  staff    6368 Sep  2 22:20 node_modules\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff  128716 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.bom.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   70138 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.cli.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff  108025 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.compiler.parser.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   69163 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   61486 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.compiler.serializer.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   23126 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.compiler.validator.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   74627 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.framework.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   41895 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.lsp.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   77739 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.target.blockdoc.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   46980 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.target.fatblock.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   40548 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.target.xsd.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--    1 pksoftware  staff   15146 Aug 26 21:13 org.blockml.bml.workspace.Library.fat.bml\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff  143886 Sep  3 00:13 package-lock.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff    3003 Sep  3 00:10 package.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@  18 pksoftware  staff     576 Sep  3 00:06 packages\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 pksoftware  staff     160 Aug 20 04:36 schemas\ndrwxr-xr-x@   9 pksoftware  staff     288 Aug 22 22:36 scripts\ndrwxr-xr-x@   7 pksoftware  staff     224 Aug 20 04:58 tests\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff     432 Aug 19 21:29 tsconfig.base.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff     637 Sep  3 00:10 tsconfig.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 pksoftware  staff     223 Aug 19 23:43 vitest.config.ts\nUsage: blockml &lt;command> [options]\n       blockml --help\n\nblockml is the BlockML toolchain CLI.\n\nBML is the editable source of truth. Companions (TypeScript, HTML, XSD, …) are derived.\nChange BML first, then compile or edit companions to match. Do not invent model semantics.\n\nInvocation: npx blockml &lt;command>\nDo not install or upgrade @blockml/cli unless asked. If the CLI is missing, run npm ci.\nIf @blockml/cli is not a project dependency, report that and stop.\n\nDiscover the model with the CLI, not grep:\n  search    where something is (find FQNs)\n  inspect   give me this Block already resolved (effective members)\n  graph     how it connects (inheritance, uses, used-by)\nGeneric grep, find, and file reads remain allowed. They are not the first way into the model.\n\nWorkflow:\n  task → search → FQNs → inspect (graph if structure) → targeted BML read → smallest BML edit → validate\n       → update companions to match (compile and/or edit)\n\nCommands:\n  search      Find FQNs. Corpus is validate --all.\n              blockml search &lt;query> [--json] [--limit n]\n              blockml search index [--force]\n  inspect     Resolved Block JSON (effective members).\n              blockml inspect &lt;fqn> [--depth n]\n  graph       Inheritance, uses / used-by, members, paths.\n              blockml graph uses|used-by|neighbors|ancestors|descendants|members &lt;fqn>\n              blockml graph path &lt;from> &lt;to>\n              blockml graph query &lt;cypher> | schema | index\n  new         Create a Block .bml and export it from the owning Library.\n              blockml new &lt;fqn> [--baseType FQN] [--is text]\n  validate    Parser + semantic check. Default: project sources, not npm.\n              blockml validate [--all] [&lt;file>]\n  compile     Render derived output for a registered target.\n              blockml compile blockdoc|xsd|fatblock\n  transform   Run a pending ModelTransformation.\n              blockml transform apply &lt;execution-fqn>\n\nShared flags: --src dir, --libraries a,b, --json, --help / -h\nCorpus for search, inspect, and graph is the same as validate --all.\nExit codes: 0 success, 1 diagnostic errors, 2 usage or configuration error.\n\nRun `blockml &lt;command> --help` for flags, defaults, output, and constraints.&quot;,&quot;stderr&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;interrupted&quot;:false,&quot;isImage&quot;:false,&quot;noOutputExpected&quot;:false}}
